1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,350
Last time, wood floated and metal sank: the material matters.

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:08,320
A giant metal ship floats, because of the trapped air inside.

3
00:00:08,610 --> 00:00:10,430
Now, test two: the rain!

4
00:00:13,682 --> 00:00:14,912
Lock in first.

5
00:00:15,162 --> 00:00:17,622
A little snail is hiding in this video.

6
00:00:17,872 --> 00:00:19,112
Can you spot it?

7
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:20,986
Today you'll learn:

8
00:00:21,189 --> 00:00:22,749
What waterproof means.

9
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:25,080
Waterproof or not waterproof.

10
00:00:25,285 --> 00:00:27,355
Wax makes fabric waterproof.

11
00:00:29,043 --> 00:00:29,923
Round one.

12
00:00:30,233 --> 00:00:33,113
A plastic raincoat, and a fabric school shoe.

13
00:00:33,393 --> 00:00:35,373
One drop of water lands on each.

14
00:00:35,643 --> 00:00:37,593
Which one does the water soak into?

15
00:00:37,903 --> 00:00:39,193
One, the raincoat.

16
00:00:39,463 --> 00:00:40,483
Two, the shoe.

17
00:00:40,783 --> 00:00:41,793
Three, both.

18
00:00:42,073 --> 00:00:43,553
Show me with your fingers.

19
00:00:49,027 --> 00:00:50,007
Locked in!

20
00:00:50,135 --> 00:00:50,815
Three!

21
00:00:51,105 --> 00:00:51,885
Both!

22
00:00:51,955 --> 00:00:53,805
Rain makes everything wet!

23
00:00:53,853 --> 00:00:54,463
Two!

24
00:00:54,643 --> 00:00:56,293
My socks were wet all day!

25
00:00:56,346 --> 00:00:57,136
Two.

26
00:00:57,906 --> 00:00:59,036
Look closer.

27
00:00:59,646 --> 00:01:01,546
A drop lands on the raincoat.

28
00:01:02,126 --> 00:01:04,616
It sits on top, round like a bead.

29
00:01:04,962 --> 00:01:05,912
Tilt it.

30
00:01:06,492 --> 00:01:07,922
The drop rolls off.

31
00:01:08,502 --> 00:01:10,032
The plastic is dry.

32
00:01:10,937 --> 00:01:12,007
Now the shoe.

33
00:01:12,597 --> 00:01:14,947
The drop soaks in, between the threads.

34
00:01:15,507 --> 00:01:16,987
A wet patch spreads.

35
00:01:17,202 --> 00:01:19,572
The fabric absorbs the water.

36
00:01:20,462 --> 00:01:21,742
And look inside.

37
00:01:22,332 --> 00:01:23,922
The water passes through.

38
00:01:24,502 --> 00:01:25,642
A wet sock!

39
00:01:28,513 --> 00:01:29,823
The answer is two.

40
00:01:30,093 --> 00:01:30,983
The shoe!

41
00:01:31,031 --> 00:01:31,621
Oh!

42
00:01:31,921 --> 00:01:34,031
No water went into the raincoat!

43
00:01:34,084 --> 00:01:35,114
Two fingers?

44
00:01:35,384 --> 00:01:36,604
One finger up!

45
00:01:37,927 --> 00:01:39,177
Say it with me!

46
00:01:39,887 --> 00:01:43,457
Materials that do not absorb water at all are waterproof.

47
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:51,590
Fabric absorbs water and allows water to pass through it.

48
00:01:51,870 --> 00:01:53,900
It is not a waterproof material.

49
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:55,770
Be a raindrop!

50
00:01:56,070 --> 00:01:57,070
Shrink down.

51
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:58,280
Quietly.

52
00:02:00,562 --> 00:02:03,412
You are a raindrop, falling past the flats.

53
00:02:04,085 --> 00:02:04,975
Splat!

54
00:02:05,745 --> 00:02:07,845
You land on a plastic raincoat.

55
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:09,790
You cannot get in.

56
00:02:10,610 --> 00:02:12,800
You roll off, onto a fabric shoe.

57
00:02:13,462 --> 00:02:15,832
Now you soak in, between the threads.

58
00:02:16,501 --> 00:02:18,111
The fabric absorbs you.

59
00:02:18,891 --> 00:02:20,391
You pass right through!

60
00:02:22,668 --> 00:02:27,168
Rubber, plastic, glass and metals do not absorb water and do not

61
00:02:27,188 --> 00:02:28,948
allow water to pass through them.

62
00:02:29,228 --> 00:02:31,108
They are waterproof materials.

63
00:02:31,847 --> 00:02:33,937
Can a fabric boot keep water out?

64
00:02:34,217 --> 00:02:35,327
Look closer.

65
00:02:35,682 --> 00:02:37,122
Two fabric boots.

66
00:02:37,702 --> 00:02:40,242
A hand rubs shoe wax over one.

67
00:02:40,802 --> 00:02:41,942
A thin layer.

68
00:02:42,741 --> 00:02:44,151
One drop on each.

69
00:02:44,751 --> 00:02:46,801
On the plain boot, it soaks in.

70
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:49,580
On the boot with wax, it sits on top.

71
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,360
It rolls off!

72
00:02:54,406 --> 00:02:55,786
The same fabric.

73
00:02:56,026 --> 00:02:57,396
A new property!

74
00:02:58,501 --> 00:02:59,651
Say it with me!

75
00:03:00,365 --> 00:03:01,845
Fabric absorbs water.

76
00:03:02,425 --> 00:03:05,855
However, it can be made waterproof by applying a layer of wax

77
00:03:05,875 --> 00:03:06,705
over it.

78
00:03:09,335 --> 00:03:12,905
The physical property of a material can change according to how the

79
00:03:12,925 --> 00:03:14,415
material is treated.

80
00:03:16,225 --> 00:03:17,045
My notes!

81
00:03:17,135 --> 00:03:18,785
One: glass is waterproof.

82
00:03:18,845 --> 00:03:21,805
Two: my T-shirt dries fast, so it is waterproof.

83
00:03:22,025 --> 00:03:24,255
Three: wax makes fabric waterproof.

84
00:03:24,530 --> 00:03:25,430
Showdown!

85
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:26,870
Double points.

86
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:28,760
One line has a mistake.

87
00:03:29,050 --> 00:03:30,810
Line one, two, or three?

88
00:03:31,110 --> 00:03:32,580
Show me with your fingers.

89
00:03:39,055 --> 00:03:40,035
Locked in!

90
00:03:40,163 --> 00:03:40,543
Two.

91
00:03:40,563 --> 00:03:42,913
A T-shirt is fabric.

92
00:03:43,063 --> 00:03:44,883
Fabric absorbs water.

93
00:03:44,936 --> 00:03:45,586
Two!

94
00:03:45,837 --> 00:03:46,497
Oops!

95
00:03:46,993 --> 00:03:50,043
Waterproof means it does not absorb water at all.

96
00:03:50,333 --> 00:03:52,073
A T-shirt absorbs water!

97
00:03:52,198 --> 00:03:53,238
Two fingers?

98
00:03:53,478 --> 00:03:55,408
Put up two more on your score hand!

99
00:03:55,966 --> 00:03:57,071
Say it with us!

100
00:03:57,731 --> 00:03:58,949
Float or sink?

101
00:03:59,311 --> 00:04:00,760
The material matters!

102
00:04:04,131 --> 00:04:05,181
Metal ship!

103
00:04:05,711 --> 00:04:07,169
Trapped air inside!

104
00:04:10,531 --> 00:04:11,291
Waterproof!

105
00:04:11,311 --> 00:04:13,205
Does not absorb water at all!

106
00:04:17,686 --> 00:04:19,156
Show me your score hand!

107
00:04:19,436 --> 00:04:20,486
More than one?

108
00:04:20,786 --> 00:04:22,146
You beat the Buddies.

109
00:04:22,446 --> 00:04:23,506
Three fingers?

110
00:04:23,776 --> 00:04:24,786
High five!

111
00:04:25,291 --> 00:04:26,721
Did you spot the snail?

112
00:04:27,011 --> 00:04:28,781
It was on the big flower pot!

113
00:04:29,051 --> 00:04:30,351
Tell someone at home.

114
00:04:31,138 --> 00:04:32,458
Next time, light!

115
00:04:32,728 --> 00:04:35,088
Which one lets only some light pass through?

116
00:04:35,368 --> 00:04:36,768
One, clear glass.

117
00:04:37,048 --> 00:04:38,608
Two, frosted glass.

118
00:04:38,898 --> 00:04:40,418
Three, a wooden door.

119
00:04:40,718 --> 00:04:42,038
Lock in your answer!

120
00:04:42,088 --> 00:04:43,768
I can hide behind all three!

121
00:04:43,878 --> 00:04:44,768
Can I?

122
00:04:45,492 --> 00:04:47,692
Let's read today's key words together!

123
00:04:47,982 --> 00:04:48,742
Ready?

124
00:04:49,029 --> 00:04:49,949
Absorb.

125
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:52,400
Waterproof.

126
00:04:54,013 --> 00:04:54,667
Wax.

127
00:04:56,021 --> 00:04:56,961
Well done!

128
00:04:57,943 --> 00:04:59,044
Say it with us!

129
00:04:59,844 --> 00:05:00,594
Ready?

130
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:01,377
One!

131
00:05:01,717 --> 00:05:02,417
two!

132
00:05:02,722 --> 00:05:03,897
Now you know!
